Aerie-Purpose: Put the Aerie window frame under everything in BrowserView and let Helium's frame fills paint nothing while it is on.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui/views/frame (browser_view.*, themed_background.cc, multi_contents_background_view.cc, BUILD.gn)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #178. The view itself (FrameTintView, its own opaque ui::Layer, painted on state change only)
and the question "is the tint on" are in the overlay, chrome/browser/ui/views/aerie_frame; the
palette and the paint are in components/aerie_frame.

- browser_view.*: a normal window with the sidebar layout creates FrameTintView as its first child,
  before the main background region, so it is the lowest layer. It is created in the constructor,
  with the window, and given the contents container as the page card once that exists.
  frame_tint_view_for_testing() is for the browser tests.
- themed_background.cc: PaintBackground() paints nothing for the frame colour while the tint is on.
  CustomCornersBackground (the sidebar's column, the corners) and MultiContentsBackgroundView paint
  the frame colour through it. The toolbar colour is not touched: split view's mini toolbar and the
  side panel still need it.
- multi_contents_background_view.cc: the gutter around the card is the tint, so while it is on the
  view is a transparent textured layer, as it is with native frame materials (one local helper
  names the condition).


